      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Generally, news coverage often uses more neutral or activist-oriented language for protests, such as describing participants as \"citizens\" or using terms like \"advocacy.\" Conversely, coverage of riots tends to employ more loaded, negative language, frequently labeling participants as \"rioters,\" \"mobs,\" or focusing heavily on property damage. The framing of the issue also shifts: white suburban protests are often framed around policy and rights, while urban minority protests are frequently framed around social justice and systemic issues.",
